 وَسْـَٔلُوا۟ مَآ أَنفَقْتُمْ وَلْيَسْـَٔلُوا۟ مَآ أَنفَقُوا۟ ۚ ذَٰلِكُمْ حُكْمُ ٱللَّهِ ۖ يَحْكُمُ بَيْنَكُمْ ۚ وَٱللَّهُ عَلِيمٌ حَكِيمٌ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"You who believe, test the believing women when they come to you as emigrants- God knows best about their faith- and if you are sure of their belief, do not send them back to the disbelievers: they are not lawful wives for them, nor are the disbelievers their lawful husbands. Give the disbelievers whatever bride-gifts they have paid- if you choose to marry them, there is no blame on you once you have paid their bride-gifts- and do not yourselves hold on to marriage ties with disbelieving women. Ask for repayment of the bride-gifts you have paid, and let the disbelievers do the same. This is God’s judgement: He judges between you, God is all knowing and wise.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"يَـٰٓأَيُّهَا","en_gloss":"O you","transliteration":"yāayyuhā","verse_key":"60:10"},{"pos":2,"ar":"ٱلَّذِينَ","en_gloss":"who","transliteration":"alladhīna","verse_key":"60:10"},{"pos":3,"ar":"ءَامَنُوٓا۟","en_gloss":"believe","transliteration":"āmanū","verse_key":"60:10"},{"pos":4,"ar":"إِذَا","en_gloss":"When","transliteration":"idhā","verse_key":"60:10"},{"pos":5,"ar":"جَآءَكُمُ","en_gloss":"come to you","transliteration":"jāakumu","verse_key":"60:10"},{"pos":6,"ar":"ٱلْمُؤْمِنَـٰتُ","en_gloss":"the believing women","transliteration":"l-mu'minātu","verse_key":"60:10"},{"pos":7,"ar":"مُهَـٰجِرَٰتٍۢ","en_gloss":"(as) emigrants","transliteration":"muhājirātin","verse_key":"60:10"},{"pos":8,"ar":"فَٱمْتَحِنُوهُنَّ ۖ","en_gloss":"then examine them","transliteration":"fa-im'taḥinūhunna","verse_key":"60:10"},{"pos":9,"ar":"ٱللَّهُ","en_gloss":"Allah","transliteration":"l-lahu","verse_key":"60:10"},{"pos":10,"ar":"أَعْلَمُ","en_gloss":"(is) most knowing","transliteration":"aʿlamu","verse_key":"60:10"},{"pos":11,"ar":"بِإِيمَـٰنِهِنَّ ۖ","en_gloss":"of their faith","transliteration":"biīmānihinna","verse_key":"60:10"},{"pos":